-- 168 bits. The variable arm's rest as a parser call on the same stream with
-- the tail as continuation: list (\q. intL) list = intL list1 list
-- = list1 list1 (intL list1 list) = (K N) (...) = N. Productive because the
-- inner call sits in the skip's erased operand.
(\x. x x) (\x. (\intL. \cont. \list.
  list (\a. a) (\u. list (\q. cont) (list (\q. intL) list))
    (\bit1. intL (\exp. bit1
      (cont (\args \arg. exp (\zx \zy. zx arg (zy args))))
      (intL (\exp2. cont (\args. exp args (exp2 args)))))))
  (x x))
